A||||5||curtis||reverse lights||||5||
Z||000000||curtis||02-21-2000||11:32 PM||||I have an 86gt. When I go into reverse and hold the shifter to the left the light will stay on if I let the shifter rest to the right the reverse lights go out. Can any one help me with this?||||reg||5
Z||000001||DXR_DAD||02-21-2000||11:51 PM||||Adjustment screw is on the reverse switch, located on the linkage, under the shift boot.<BR>There is a little screw at the end of the switch button, turn it to make contact with the reverse lever on the linkage.<P>This should be a quick repair.||||reg||1
Z||000002||batboy||02-22-2000||12:44 AM||||Thanks Dad, saves me having to ask, I'm having the same problem.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Carrolles||02-22-2000||11:44 PM||||I don't believe that adjusting the screw will help.  It only adjusts to compensate for front/back travel of the shifter.  The problem you are having (I also have this problem on my 85SE v-6 4spd) is that the stops that keep the shift stick in the reverse lock position (not the transmission, only the shift stick) are not holding.  It lets the shift stick slip over to the first gear position thus moving away from the reverse light switch.  I believe friction is the only thing that holds the stick over to the left, or maybe a detent in the track it slides up on to get to reverse is worn.<P>Anyway if you find that I'm wrong please let me know because I've looked at mine a lot trying to come up with a fix other than replacing the shifter.<P>Good luck,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000004||DXR_DAD||02-23-2000||12:38 AM||||Should have stated, this was the fix to my problem.<P>It did not come out of reverse. When you held the shifter all the way over (to left) in reverse the light would come on, if you did not hold it, on lights.<P>I went back in Search, this may help: <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/000918.html" TARGET=_blank>www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/000918.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Bruce||02-23-2000||01:04 AM||||Mine did the same thing until I had the shift cables adjusted, which also made shifting much easier.||||reg||1
